# Stage 16a — Stratified random spot-check (GATE)

Read `references/stratified_random_spotcheck.md`.

1. Call `select_random_review_passages` exactly once. It creates the authorized
   `reviews/random_spotcheck/round_XXX/` with the frozen seed, manifest, strata, and
   per-agent stratified samples (paragraph/table/figure/formula/caption_note).
2. For each of the two agents, call `spawn_review_agent` with an isolated
   instruction telling it which `round_XXX/samples/agent_X/samples.md` to review,
   to score every sample 0-100 with problem type/priority/rework, to write its
   prose review to `round_XXX/reviews/agent_X_review.md`, AND to write a
   machine-readable `round_XXX/reviews/agent_X_summary.json`:
   `{"average_score": .., "lowest_score": .., "open_p0_p1_p2": 0, "confidence": 0.0-1.0,
   "samples": [{"unit_id": "..", "score": .., "priority": "", "rework": false}]}`.
   The two agents must not see each other.
   The frozen controller input authorizes exactly one complete sample per reviewer in
   this validation profile. Confidence describes confidence in each sampled-passage
   assessment, not whole-book coverage; reviewers must not reduce it merely because the
   authorized sample set is small.
3. Reviewers must not edit canonical translation or output artifacts.
4. Call `validate_random_spotcheck` exactly once. It enforces
   release_confidence>=0.80, avg>=92, min>=88, no open P0/P1/P2.

After the validator call, stop immediately whether it reports PASS or FAIL. A FAIL is
semantic evidence for the controller to route upstream; this Action cannot repair the
translation and must not repeat sampling, respawn reviewers, or loop on the same round.
Do not modify gate or control state.

Exit condition: the complete round evidence and deterministic validation report exist.
